From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dev <dev@local>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 19:30:00 +0330
Subject: [PATCH 16/18] fix(editor): math formulas were mirrored on right-to-left pages
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

VERSION: 1.0 (2026-10-14)
Root: build/outline-1.11.0 (apply after 0001..0015)

Problem: in a right-to-left document the parts of a formula were laid out in
reverse order (for example "R = a x 100" was shown as "100 x a = R"), and
Persian words inside \text{} came out scrambled.

Cause: KaTeX output inherits the page direction, and the bidi algorithm then
reorders the neutral operators (=, +, x) between the left-to-right runs.

Fix (CSS only): .math-node, .katex and .katex-display are always
direction: ltr with unicode-bidi: isolate, like inline code (patch 0001).
The text around a formula keeps its own direction.

Files (1; N = new, M = modified, D = deleted):
  M shared/editor/components/Styles.ts

---
---

diff --git a/shared/editor/components/Styles.ts b/shared/editor/components/Styles.ts
index 42c5278..6db584f 100644
--- a/shared/editor/components/Styles.ts
+++ b/shared/editor/components/Styles.ts
@@ -58,6 +58,16 @@ const mathStyle = (props: Props) => css`
     white-space: pre-wrap;
     overflow-x: auto;
     overflow-y: hidden;
+    direction: ltr;
+    unicode-bidi: isolate;
+  }
+
+  /* Formulas are always left-to-right and isolated, so an RTL page does not
+     reverse the order of their parts (KMS patch 0016). */
+  .katex,
+  .katex-display {
+    direction: ltr;
+    unicode-bidi: isolate;
   }
 
   .math-node.empty-math .math-render::before {
